WEBVTT

00:00:01.790 --> 00:00:04.850
The third Heart Piece...

00:00:05.980 --> 00:00:11.210
Why doesn’t it fit?

00:00:11.210 --> 00:00:14.740
I went through a lot of trouble
to get the third Heart Piece!

00:00:14.740 --> 00:00:17.330
That would be too easy.

00:00:18.070 --> 00:00:23.920
Heart Pieces have different shapes,
and only a certain set fits perfectly.

00:00:24.750 --> 00:00:28.380
Really? This is impossible!

00:00:29.020 --> 00:00:34.090
Yuma, it’s more important
that you find an opponent with a Number.

00:00:34.090 --> 00:00:38.860
We entered the Duel Carnival in order
to retrieve Numbers.

00:00:38.860 --> 00:00:41.060
That’s your problem!

00:00:41.570 --> 00:00:44.230
You’re just always floating around and—

00:00:50.540 --> 00:00:51.110
Kotori!

00:00:57.050 --> 00:00:58.070
I missed.

00:00:59.070 --> 00:01:03.040
That was incredible for augmented reality!

00:01:03.040 --> 00:01:06.750
You’re wrong, Yuma! It was real!

00:01:07.370 --> 00:01:08.920
I won’t miss this time!

00:01:12.880 --> 00:01:14.390
This way!

00:01:16.590 --> 00:01:18.260
Stop moving around!

00:01:18.640 --> 00:01:20.380
What?

00:01:20.380 --> 00:01:22.760
It seems you’re the target.

00:01:22.760 --> 00:01:24.890
That’s impossible!

00:01:24.890 --> 00:01:26.600
This way, Kotori!

00:01:30.440 --> 00:01:32.820
Stop underestimating me!

00:01:34.210 --> 00:01:36.860
Do you think you
can escape from me?

00:01:43.890 --> 00:01:47.250
Here I go! Flying Launcher—

00:02:05.930 --> 00:02:08.470
Stop!

00:02:08.470 --> 00:02:11.060
We really are the targets!

00:02:12.000 --> 00:02:13.820
Who is that?

00:02:13.820 --> 00:02:16.490
Out of the way!

00:02:17.700 --> 00:02:19.820
Take this!

00:02:21.430 --> 00:02:22.870
This way!

00:02:48.810 --> 00:02:52.270
We’ve run far away,
so we should be safe.

00:02:53.760 --> 00:02:55.020
This is the end!

00:02:56.690 --> 00:02:59.680
You can no longer escape—

00:03:06.950 --> 00:03:09.350
I reached my hand towards

00:03:09.350 --> 00:03:12.530
The light that shines to tomorrow

00:03:12.530 --> 00:03:19.470
I dreamed of the world
that spreads beneath my feet

00:03:23.380 --> 00:03:28.310
I don’t know where dreams
and hope are located

00:03:29.180 --> 00:03:33.150
No matter how much I search,
I can’t find them

00:03:34.440 --> 00:03:39.610
Maybe it fell into
the space between truth and lies

00:03:39.670 --> 00:03:44.910
Our story hasn’t started yet

00:03:44.910 --> 00:03:50.200
The road to tomorrow
seems like it will crumble

00:03:50.200 --> 00:03:55.710
But let’s go
before we lose heart

00:03:55.710 --> 00:03:58.460
As we come closer,
it moves further away

00:03:58.550 --> 00:04:01.630
In order to seize the truth

00:04:01.630 --> 00:04:06.970
We’ll search for hope
in the unseen future

00:04:06.970 --> 00:04:09.720
Our hearts are stronger
than everyone else’s

00:04:09.720 --> 00:04:12.850
We’ll carry it
within us and go

00:04:12.850 --> 00:04:18.070
Fight weakness to have
the strength to win

00:04:18.520 --> 00:04:20.280
In order to find it

00:04:20.710 --> 00:04:23.610
Along with my irreplaceable friends

00:04:23.740 --> 00:04:30.700
I saw tomorrow in the world
that spreads beneath my feet

00:04:37.600 --> 00:04:39.300
Umm...

00:04:39.880 --> 00:04:42.310
I won’t let you escape!

00:04:42.310 --> 00:04:43.590
Are you ready?

00:04:43.590 --> 00:04:48.050
\hThe Railroad Deck Takes Off! The Rowdy Duelist, Anna\h

00:04:43.590 --> 00:04:48.050
Number 29:

00:04:43.590 --> 00:04:48.050
Wait a second! What’s going on?

00:04:49.250 --> 00:04:53.690
You never know when
to give up, Yuma Tsukumo!

00:04:53.690 --> 00:04:55.900
You’re Anna!

00:04:55.900 --> 00:04:57.000
Anna?

00:04:57.000 --> 00:04:59.480
Yeah, remember? Anna Kozuki!

00:04:59.920 --> 00:05:07.280
She transferred two years ago,
but she always fought boys and protected bullying victims.

00:05:07.280 --> 00:05:08.970
That’s Anna!

00:05:08.970 --> 00:05:11.200
I don’t remember her at all.

00:05:11.620 --> 00:05:14.830
In that case,
I’ll make you remember!

00:05:18.140 --> 00:05:21.860
I remember! I remember now!

00:05:22.710 --> 00:05:25.600
But why are you attacking Yuma?

00:05:25.600 --> 00:05:27.890
For revenge, of course!

00:05:27.890 --> 00:05:29.220
Revenge?

00:05:29.590 --> 00:05:33.950
Yuma Tsukumo,
don’t you know that I...

00:05:35.930 --> 00:05:39.190
I said, don’t
you know that I...

00:05:39.970 --> 00:05:41.150
Whatever!

00:05:41.790 --> 00:05:44.150
Does Anna like Yuma?

00:05:45.180 --> 00:05:46.320
That’s why I...

00:05:46.320 --> 00:05:48.660
What’s going on?

00:05:50.030 --> 00:05:52.740
That’s why I glued your shoes.

00:05:54.120 --> 00:05:56.710
And drew all over your D-Pad.

00:05:58.040 --> 00:06:00.540
And cut holes
in your swim trunks.

00:06:01.490 --> 00:06:04.510
And put rocks
in your rice balls.

00:06:04.870 --> 00:06:07.910
That’s horrible.

00:06:07.910 --> 00:06:10.220
I mean, I remember that.

00:06:10.710 --> 00:06:15.350
So you remember! But I had to
transfer two years ago.

00:06:15.350 --> 00:06:22.690
That’s why I asked you to meet me
before I transferred so that I could confess my love!

00:06:26.090 --> 00:06:28.320
But you didn’t come.

00:06:29.330 --> 00:06:31.900
Even though you
knew how I felt.

00:06:38.850 --> 00:06:44.420
You will pay for this!

00:06:45.420 --> 00:06:51.680
I’ll be nice. I’ll end you
in a single shot so that you won’t suffer!

00:06:53.480 --> 00:06:54.600
Wait!

00:06:55.120 --> 00:06:59.560
I know how you feel,
but you don’t need to use that!

00:06:59.560 --> 00:07:04.320
If you want revenge,
then let’s have a duel!

00:07:05.330 --> 00:07:06.980
A duel?

00:07:06.980 --> 00:07:10.850
Yuma, you know she’s
not going to accept!

00:07:10.850 --> 00:07:12.040
Fine.

00:07:12.450 --> 00:07:14.080
I’ll take you on.

00:07:14.910 --> 00:07:19.120
Knowing you, I thought
this might happen.

00:07:19.120 --> 00:07:21.040
Therefore, I also started dueling!

00:07:22.680 --> 00:07:24.590
I don’t know what’s going on.

00:07:24.590 --> 00:07:29.130
But if I win,
I get to have you!

00:07:29.620 --> 00:07:32.480
Fine! I won’t lose this duel!

00:07:32.480 --> 00:07:33.470
Yuma!

00:07:33.470 --> 00:07:35.640
Let’s battle, Yuma Tsukumo!

00:07:36.220 --> 00:07:38.620
Duel Disk set!

00:07:38.620 --> 00:07:41.350
D-Gazer set!

00:07:42.430 --> 00:07:45.320
AR Vision Link complete.

00:07:46.800 --> 00:07:48.500
Duel!

00:07:48.500 --> 00:07:53.410
Human love is beyond my understanding.

00:07:55.620 --> 00:07:59.870
I’ll go first!
My turn! I draw!

00:07:59.870 --> 00:08:04.000
I Special Summon Rocket Arrow Express!

00:08:11.930 --> 00:08:14.130
5000 ATK?

00:08:14.130 --> 00:08:16.390
That’s insane!

00:08:17.050 --> 00:08:20.350
She already Special Summoned
a heavyweight monster!

00:08:20.350 --> 00:08:27.690
This card can’t be Normal Summoned, but I can Special
Summon it from my hand when I have no cards on my field.

00:08:27.690 --> 00:08:33.820
Every time it’s my turn, it’ll be destroyed
unless I send five cards in my hand to the graveyard.

00:08:34.370 --> 00:08:39.790
Five cards? If you send that many to the graveyard,
you’ll quickly run out of cards in your hand!

00:08:39.790 --> 00:08:45.120
When I Special Summon Rocket Arrow
Express, I can’t attack that turn.

00:08:45.120 --> 00:08:49.990
And when it’s on the field,
I can’t set any other card.

00:08:49.990 --> 00:08:54.010
I end my turn!
Now bring it!

00:08:55.070 --> 00:08:57.360
My turn! I draw!

00:08:57.360 --> 00:08:58.800
Yuma.

00:08:58.800 --> 00:09:01.470
You won’t be able to
destroy Rocket Arrow this turn.

00:09:01.840 --> 00:09:05.230
Yeah, so I’ll prepare
for the next turn.

00:09:05.230 --> 00:09:09.110
I set a monster
in defense position!

00:09:09.110 --> 00:09:12.570
Then I set one card
and end my turn!

00:09:12.570 --> 00:09:15.370
You’re afraid to face me!

00:09:15.370 --> 00:09:17.570
No, I’m not!

00:09:18.520 --> 00:09:23.250
Just watch! My turn! I draw!

00:09:23.610 --> 00:09:27.540
I won’t pay the cost,
so Rocket Arrow is destroyed!

00:09:29.110 --> 00:09:30.040
What?

00:09:30.590 --> 00:09:34.130
I set five cards
and end my turn!

00:09:37.200 --> 00:09:39.640
You’re setting five cards this time?

00:09:39.640 --> 00:09:43.770
Since she doesn’t have any
monsters, she’s unguarded!

00:09:43.770 --> 00:09:45.640
What is she planning?

00:09:45.640 --> 00:09:48.600
Now bring it on!

00:09:49.960 --> 00:09:51.950
There’s no point thinking about it!

00:09:51.950 --> 00:09:54.240
My turn! I draw!

00:09:54.240 --> 00:09:57.320
I summon Gogogo Giant!

00:10:01.410 --> 00:10:04.750
Gogogo Giant attacks you directly!

00:10:04.750 --> 00:10:08.840
If this works, you take
2000 points of damage!

00:10:08.840 --> 00:10:10.380
Go!

00:10:10.860 --> 00:10:14.130
Wait, Yuma! She
has five set cards!

00:10:14.130 --> 00:10:18.200
I destroy all my set cards!

00:10:19.090 --> 00:10:20.050
What?

00:10:20.050 --> 00:10:25.080
I Special Summon Snow
Plow Hustle Rustle!

00:10:25.900 --> 00:10:28.300
This card can’t be Normal Summoned.

00:10:28.300 --> 00:10:37.290
When you attack me directly, I can Special Summon it
from my hand by destroying all my spell and trap cards!

00:10:38.300 --> 00:10:42.320
Appear, Snow Plow Hustle Rustle!

00:10:42.830 --> 00:10:45.560
2500 ATK?

00:10:45.560 --> 00:10:48.970
Gogogo Giant, don’t battle!

00:10:50.130 --> 00:10:51.210
You’re scared!

00:10:51.210 --> 00:10:53.710
In that case,
I’ll take the offensive!

00:10:53.710 --> 00:10:57.920
I activate Snow Plow
Hustle Rustle’s effect!

00:10:57.920 --> 00:11:04.530
For every spell and trap card that was destroyed,
you take 200 points of damage!

00:11:04.530 --> 00:11:07.140
Since there were five cards,
that’s 1000 points!

00:11:15.810 --> 00:11:17.070
Yuma!

00:11:17.070 --> 00:11:21.530
All right! I already dealt
1000 points of damage!

00:11:22.750 --> 00:11:25.580
Her plan was
to deal effect damage.

00:11:25.580 --> 00:11:27.540
What’s with this duel?

00:11:28.300 --> 00:11:33.250
It looked like she was playing randomly,
but she actually calculated everything.

00:11:34.230 --> 00:11:36.160
Be careful, Yuma.

00:11:36.160 --> 00:11:38.810
Her strength is extraordinary.

00:11:38.810 --> 00:11:42.320
Be quiet! I just
had my guard down!

00:11:42.320 --> 00:11:43.550
I end my turn!

00:11:43.550 --> 00:11:45.270
All right! Here I go!

00:11:45.270 --> 00:11:45.760
Yuma...

00:11:46.280 --> 00:11:48.810
My turn! I draw!

00:11:50.060 --> 00:11:53.800
I activate the spell
card Special Schedule!

00:11:56.150 --> 00:12:03.990
I can Special Summon a Machine-Type monster
with at least 3000 ATK from my graveyard in defense position!

00:12:03.990 --> 00:12:08.780
Resurrect, Rocket Arrow Express!

00:12:10.230 --> 00:12:12.820
That monster again?

00:12:12.820 --> 00:12:14.880
She has two Level 10 monsters.

00:12:15.290 --> 00:12:18.210
Yuma, here I come
with my raucous deck!

00:12:18.760 --> 00:12:21.670
Try to stop me
if you can!

00:12:21.670 --> 00:12:27.110
I overlay Level 10 Rocket Arrow
and Hustle Rustle!

00:12:27.930 --> 00:12:32.060
With these two monsters,
I build the Overlay Network!

00:12:32.810 --> 00:12:34.650
Xyz Summon!

00:12:35.140 --> 00:12:40.990
Appear, Superdreadnought
Rail Cannon Gustav Max!

00:12:48.140 --> 00:12:50.740
3000 ATK!

00:12:50.740 --> 00:12:53.580
And it’s a Rank 10 Xyz Monster.

00:12:53.580 --> 00:12:56.960
Feel its power!

00:12:56.960 --> 00:13:01.180
I activate Gustav Max’s effect!

00:13:04.090 --> 00:13:12.140
Once per turn, it can use one Overlay Unit
to deal 2000 points of damage!

00:13:17.000 --> 00:13:18.910
It transformed?

00:13:18.910 --> 00:13:21.730
And 2000 points of damage?

00:13:21.730 --> 00:13:24.700
Go, Gustav Max!

00:13:24.700 --> 00:13:27.700
Big Cannon is ready to fire!

00:13:36.040 --> 00:13:40.000
I did it!

00:13:40.000 --> 00:13:43.840
You have 1000 LP left!

00:13:44.380 --> 00:13:46.550
This duel is mine!

00:13:46.550 --> 00:13:49.970
Don’t forget your promise!

00:13:49.970 --> 00:13:51.100
This is the end!

00:13:51.750 --> 00:13:58.560
Gustav Max has 3000 ATK,
and it attacks Gogogo Giant that has 2000 ATK!

00:14:04.570 --> 00:14:05.740
Yuma!

00:14:10.320 --> 00:14:11.700
Yuma!

00:14:11.700 --> 00:14:15.140
I activate the trap Overlay Buster!

00:14:15.550 --> 00:14:22.130
One monster on the field gains 500 ATK
until the end of the Battle Phase.

00:14:28.850 --> 00:14:30.270
I end my turn.

00:14:30.270 --> 00:14:31.760
You managed to survive.

00:14:32.240 --> 00:14:34.720
But it’s over next turn!

00:14:35.180 --> 00:14:37.120
What should I do?

00:14:37.120 --> 00:14:40.690
Unless I do something,
I’ll take Gustav Max’s effect and lose.

00:14:41.140 --> 00:14:46.980
But defeating Gustav Max
with its 3000 ATK isn’t easy.

00:14:47.770 --> 00:14:49.410
There is a way.

00:14:50.480 --> 00:14:52.500
How?

00:14:52.500 --> 00:14:54.340
Did you forget?

00:14:54.340 --> 00:14:56.700
Your new teammate.

00:14:58.090 --> 00:15:00.080
New?

00:15:00.080 --> 00:15:01.580
Oh yeah!

00:15:01.580 --> 00:15:04.750
I have a new teammate!

00:15:05.150 --> 00:15:08.170
My turn! I draw!

00:15:08.170 --> 00:15:10.630
I summon Zubaba Knight!

00:15:14.430 --> 00:15:18.310
Then I Flip Summon Rai Rider!

00:15:21.940 --> 00:15:27.060
I overlay Level 3 Zubaba
Knight and Rai Rider!

00:15:28.020 --> 00:15:34.120
With these two monsters,
I build the Overlay Network! Xyz Summon!

00:15:34.910 --> 00:15:38.160
Appear, my new teammate!

00:15:41.870 --> 00:15:45.590
Temtempo the Percussion Djinn!

00:15:46.670 --> 00:15:49.010
A monster with only 1000 DEF?

00:15:49.010 --> 00:15:51.030
Just watch!

00:15:51.030 --> 00:15:54.800
I activate Temtempo
the Percussion Djinn’s effect!

00:15:54.800 --> 00:16:02.460
It uses one Overlay Unit to send all Overlay
Units on your Xyz Monster to the graveyard!

00:16:02.460 --> 00:16:03.520
What?

00:16:03.600 --> 00:16:10.380
It also gains 500 ATK for every Overlay Unit
that was sent to the graveyard!

00:16:10.380 --> 00:16:12.610
Drumming Sonic!

00:16:12.610 --> 00:16:16.360
Now you can’t use
Gustav Max’s effect!

00:16:16.360 --> 00:16:21.040
And since Temtempo is in defense position,
you won’t take battle damage.

00:16:21.480 --> 00:16:25.040
I set two cards
and end my turn!

00:16:25.040 --> 00:16:27.710
How dare you?

00:16:27.710 --> 00:16:32.090
I’ll show you what happens
when you make me angry!

00:16:32.590 --> 00:16:34.380
My turn! I draw!

00:16:34.970 --> 00:16:39.000
I activate the Equip Spell
Train Connection from my hand!

00:16:39.560 --> 00:16:45.280
By banishing two Level 8-or-above
Machine-Type monsters from my graveyard...

00:16:45.280 --> 00:16:51.110
I can equip this card
on a Machine-Type monster to double its ATK!

00:16:51.470 --> 00:16:53.070
Double?

00:17:03.590 --> 00:17:06.380
6000 ATK!

00:17:06.380 --> 00:17:09.430
It’s stronger than Rocket Arrow!

00:17:09.430 --> 00:17:11.130
What destructive power!

00:17:11.510 --> 00:17:23.730
And when the monster equipped with Train Connection attacks
a monster in defense position, it deals piercing damage!

00:17:23.730 --> 00:17:27.230
Since Temtempo has 1000 DEF...

00:17:27.230 --> 00:17:30.980
If you attack, I’ll take
5000 points of damage!

00:17:31.520 --> 00:17:33.800
It’s over.

00:17:33.800 --> 00:17:36.280
Yuma, you’re mine!

00:17:38.490 --> 00:17:41.930
Or are you going to
cry like before?

00:17:41.930 --> 00:17:43.330
Cry?

00:17:43.330 --> 00:17:46.850
When I took your card!

00:17:46.850 --> 00:17:50.340
If you want it back,
then climb up!

00:17:50.340 --> 00:17:52.710
Please give it back!

00:17:52.710 --> 00:17:56.760
You cried because you
couldn’t climb trees.

00:17:56.760 --> 00:17:58.700
Wasn’t that...

00:17:58.700 --> 00:18:00.220
Did I do that?

00:18:00.780 --> 00:18:02.170
You’re playing dumb again?

00:18:02.170 --> 00:18:06.180
I don’t remember
what I don’t remember!

00:18:06.650 --> 00:18:12.190
I’ll make you remember
with 6000 ATK!

00:18:13.020 --> 00:18:15.390
Yuma, you have 500 LP.

00:18:15.390 --> 00:18:18.510
6000 ATK are heading your way.

00:18:18.510 --> 00:18:20.160
Stop complimenting her!

00:18:20.710 --> 00:18:23.790
But this will be her downfall.

00:18:25.250 --> 00:18:28.420
Here I go, Yuma!
I’ll finish you!

00:18:28.420 --> 00:18:29.830
I see!

00:18:29.830 --> 00:18:32.790
Go, Gustav Max!

00:18:32.790 --> 00:18:35.670
Attack Temtempo!

00:18:35.670 --> 00:18:37.130
Yuma!

00:18:38.470 --> 00:18:40.430
Gustav Hammer!

00:18:40.990 --> 00:18:44.210
I activate the trap Gamushara!

00:18:45.630 --> 00:18:52.050
When you attack my monster in defense position,
it switches to attack position before continuing the battle!

00:18:52.460 --> 00:18:57.490
2200 ATK? That’s not enough
to defeat Gustav Max!

00:18:57.900 --> 00:18:59.970
I will defeat it!

00:18:59.970 --> 00:19:02.490
I’m kattobing!

00:19:02.930 --> 00:19:06.700
I activate the trap Mirror Mail!

00:19:07.150 --> 00:19:14.250
Until the end of the Battle Phase, my monster
and your monster will have the same ATK!

00:19:14.250 --> 00:19:16.840
They have the same ATK!

00:19:30.480 --> 00:19:31.950
What?

00:19:32.940 --> 00:19:44.040
When your monster is destroyed, the trap card Gamushara
deals damage equal to your destroyed monster’s ATK!

00:19:44.040 --> 00:19:44.950
What?

00:19:44.950 --> 00:19:51.710
Go! Gamushara’s effect deals
you 6000 points of damage!

00:20:01.370 --> 00:20:03.300
I win!

00:20:09.120 --> 00:20:11.640
I lost.

00:20:12.140 --> 00:20:14.680
Why?

00:20:14.680 --> 00:20:20.320
Because you attacked with 6000 ATK
when I only had 500 LP.

00:20:22.070 --> 00:20:27.490
If you didn’t do that, Gamushara’s effect
wouldn’t have dealt you lots of damage.

00:20:28.080 --> 00:20:29.900
Damn!

00:20:30.720 --> 00:20:34.590
I don’t know if this is
the right time to ask, but...

00:20:35.520 --> 00:20:40.920
Anna, didn’t you like Yuya
Tsukune instead of Yuma?

00:20:41.630 --> 00:20:44.450
Yuya Tsukune?

00:20:44.450 --> 00:20:50.600
I remember him. He always cried
and went to the teachers’ lounge.

00:20:56.560 --> 00:20:59.020
Please give it back!

00:21:02.900 --> 00:21:05.730
It’s your fault for having
a confusing name!

00:21:05.730 --> 00:21:09.330
I’m done for today.

00:21:11.490 --> 00:21:14.080
Hey! What about the Heart Piece?

00:21:14.610 --> 00:21:16.000
Heart Piece?

00:21:16.000 --> 00:21:18.340
You gotta give it up
because you lost!

00:21:18.830 --> 00:21:21.030
What are you talking about?

00:21:21.030 --> 00:21:25.340
You’re not participating
in the Duel Carnival?

00:21:25.340 --> 00:21:27.680
Of course not!

00:21:28.510 --> 00:21:31.930
Then say so from the start!

00:21:32.570 --> 00:21:35.720
How annoying!

00:21:35.720 --> 00:21:38.580
I knew something was weird.

00:21:38.580 --> 00:21:40.810
Why would a girl like you?

00:21:40.810 --> 00:21:42.630
What?

00:21:42.630 --> 00:21:45.060
But it’s a bit unfortunate.

00:21:45.450 --> 00:21:49.570
I’ve never seen anyone duel like that.
I want to see it again.

00:21:50.120 --> 00:21:53.130
I’m fine if she
never comes back!

00:21:57.900 --> 00:22:00.120
Yuma Tsukumo...

00:22:05.550 --> 00:22:09.520
Just you wait, Yuma Tsukumo!

00:22:20.190 --> 00:22:23.350
Someone gave me water

00:22:23.720 --> 00:22:29.490
It easily created a rainbow

00:22:30.390 --> 00:22:35.190
To be
who I want to be

00:22:35.990 --> 00:22:37.930
Is difficult

00:22:39.000 --> 00:22:41.670
Without struggle

00:22:41.670 --> 00:22:45.890
I can’t win

00:22:46.570 --> 00:22:48.970
But I want to bloom

00:22:48.970 --> 00:22:53.150
I have a dream
that’s not cool

00:22:53.150 --> 00:22:56.220
In order to achieve it

00:22:56.690 --> 00:22:59.770
I don’t care
if you laugh at me

00:22:59.770 --> 00:23:06.830
I set my limits low

00:23:06.830 --> 00:23:09.820
So I’ll overcome it tomorrow

00:23:09.820 --> 00:23:13.410
Ah! Aiming for the blue skies

00:23:14.270 --> 00:23:15.630
In full bloom

00:23:15.630 --> 00:23:17.860
Yearning freesia

00:23:19.500 --> 00:23:23.400
Countless petals

00:23:23.400 --> 00:23:26.260
Were sacrificed

00:23:26.840 --> 00:23:30.090
I’m above them

00:23:30.090 --> 00:23:34.220
Ah! Lost my way again today

00:23:34.220 --> 00:23:36.100
I admire

00:23:36.100 --> 00:23:37.580
Yearning freesia

00:23:41.020 --> 00:23:42.930
A vegetable death match?

00:23:42.930 --> 00:23:46.840
The special rule states that you can’t attack
unless you eat a vegetable.

00:23:46.840 --> 00:23:48.360
I’m the poster child for tomatoes?

00:23:48.780 --> 00:23:50.970
Everything has turned into tomatoes!

00:23:50.970 --> 00:23:53.460
Yuma, why won’t you attack?

00:23:53.460 --> 00:23:56.990
The formula for victory
is complete. However...

00:23:56.990 --> 00:24:01.120
I’ll shatter your plans!

00:24:01.120 --> 00:24:09.970
\h\hYuma’s Greatest Test! A Vegetable Death Match Battle\h\h

00:24:01.120 --> 00:24:07.130
Next time on Yu-Gi-Oh! ZEXAL:
“Yuma’s Greatest Test! A Vegetable Death Match Battle”

00:24:07.130 --> 00:24:09.970
I’m kattobing!

00:24:10.460 --> 00:24:12.970
Yuma’s dueling isn’t improving.

00:24:12.970 --> 00:24:17.060
What are you talking about?
I’m much more powerful!

00:24:17.060 --> 00:24:18.640
Prove it.

00:24:18.640 --> 00:24:19.810
Fine!

00:24:19.810 --> 00:24:23.310
I Normal Summon Utopia!

00:24:23.310 --> 00:24:24.940
Are you serious?
